# The town smith: one per friendly settlement, standing at the forge in the
# stamped smithy (MapComponent_TSC_GuildFactor). Trades in silver, same
# stock as the village smith. Deliberately brief - he is a shop, not a
# character, and the named smiths (Haldor, Garrick) carry the writing.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_TownSmith

== start ==
The smith looks up from the anvil, takes in the road-dirt and the weapons, and reaches for the trade shelf without being asked.

"Buying or selling? Both's fine. Silver only - I don't take guild paper."

* "Let's trade." -> end
    do trade()
* "Some of our gear is in a bad way." -> mend
* "What's the news here?" -> news
* "Just looking." -> end

== mend ==
He wipes his hands and holds one out, palm up, without any ceremony at all.

"Bring it here. Blades, mail, boots, whatever's bitten. I'll tell you what it costs before I start, and I'll tell you if it's past me."

* "Take a look at these." -> end
    do smith_repair()
* "Another time." -> end

== news ==
He shrugs, working the bellows with one foot.

"Roads are bad. They're always bad. Steel's dear, charcoal's dearer, and every second traveler through that door has a story about something in the hills." He nods at the shelf. "I sell to all of them."

* "Let's trade, then." -> end
    do trade()
* "Then you can mend as well as sell." -> mend
* "Good day to you." -> end
